@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $4134 EnergyBarScreen ; the HUD's energy bar: screen row 1, pixel line 1, column 20
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B00 PlayBuffer 4415 ; the play buffer $5B00-$6CFF (its tail $6C3F-$6CFF is PlayBufferTail in the block): 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear; also the unpack area of StageGraphics
@equ $F959 DigitGlyphs ; resident font from '0': 8 bytes a character, 7 rows drawn (RenderDigits)
@equ $F9B0 PlaySoundVector ; resident: JP to the AY effect starter (E = the effect number)
@equ $F9BF DecimalTable 10 ; resident: the words 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1
@equ $F9CC DissolveMasks 8 ; resident: DissolveHud's eight masks
@equ $F9FB Score 2 ; resident: the score's low four decimal digits, 0-9999 (AddScore)
@equ $F9FD ScoreHigh ; resident: the score's high two digits (ten thousands), 0-99 (AddScore)
@equ $FA00 BitReverse 256 ; resident: each byte with its bits reversed (the sprites drawn facing left)
@equ $FB00 ScreenLineTable 384 ; resident: the screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (words)
@equ $FC90 KeyUp ; resident key reader: Z when UP is held (DEFINE KEYS / joystick patch its port and bit)
@equ $FC9F KeyDown ; resident key reader: Z when DOWN is held
@equ $FCAE KeyLeft ; resident key reader: Z when LEFT is held
@equ $FCBD KeyRight ; resident key reader: Z when RIGHT is held
@equ $FCCC KeyFire ; resident key reader: Z when FIRE is held
@equ $FCDB KeyHook ; resident: called before every key read (a RET, or the joystick / pause check DEFINE KEYS installs)
@equ $FE08 RandomSeed 2 ; NextSeed $909D: seed = seed x 5 + $15 (a linear congruential step); $07CF at the stage start (InitStageState)
@equ $FE0A RandomPointer 2 ; Random $90AC: a pointer into the ROM ($0000-$3FFF), whose bytes are the random numbers; reseeded from R every 64 passes, $07CF at the stage start, $0D7A at each burst
@equ $FE0E SavedSP 2 ; ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer keep the caller's SP here while SP walks their buffers
@equ $FE10 InitOnly10 ; set to 2 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE12 InitOnly12 ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE14 WorkByte ; scratch: the placement counter of LoadRoomActors, the shape bits of StartBurst
@equ $FE17 ItemSelected ; the slot of CarriedItems the HUD cursor is on (6 at the start)
@equ $FE18 ItemLast ; the last used slot of CarriedItems (6 at the start; AddItem raises it)
@equ $FE19 ItemFirst ; the first slot of CarriedItems (6): the item window does not scroll before it
@equ $FE1C RestoreAttributes ; 1: the next attribute pass ($91D0) takes the solid cells' colours from RoomAttributes once (set by SavePlayAttrs $A1A9; stage 1's $FE5A)
@equ $FE1D SpanCount 2 ; the spans in the span table $76A0 that CopyBuffer copies (BuildSpans $9959; stage 1's $FE1C)
@equ $FE1F SpanRow ; BuildSpans' cell row 0-17
@equ $FE20 CellColumn ; the cell column 2-29 of RoomChange's and BuildSpans' loops
@equ $FE22 RoomColumn ; the room's left edge in the grid, in blocks (2 cells)
@equ $FE23 RoomRow ; the room's top edge in the grid, in blocks (16 lines)
@equ $FE24 RoomGrid 2 ; the grid record of the current map grid ($9B6F, $9B8A or $9B96)
@equ $FE26 Placements 2 ; the current grid's placement list (Grid0Placements, Grid1Placements, Grid2Placements): 3 bytes a placement, $FF ends
@equ $FE28 MissileCursor ; AddMissile's round-robin slot number 0-7
@equ $FE2A CellFlag ; PutBlock $98F6: the byte written to the cell's twin in $7040 (always 0)
@equ $FE2F RoomExitsPtr 2 ; the current room's byte in the grid's room table (grid record +4 + RoomNumber)
@equ $FE31 RoomNumber ; the room in its grid, a grid row of rooms after another: +1 right, -1 left, + grid record +8 down (stage 1, grid 0: 12 the demon's lair)
@equ $FE32 PassCounter ; +1 every pass (PassTick $97BD): the animations' clock
@equ $FE36 InitOnly36 ; set to $10 by InitStageState; no stage-4 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE39 BurstTimer ; the burst's step 0..$1B ($0D in the small mode); $64 idle (RoomChange sets it), $FF just started
@equ $FE3A BurstSmall ; 0 a big burst (28 steps), 1 a small one (14 steps, doubled direction steps)
@equ $FE3B Energy ; the hero's energy, 0 (full) to $2E
@equ $FE3D InitOnly3D ; set to $0D by InitStageState; no stage-4 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE3E InitOnly3E ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-4 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE3F SpanOpen ; BuildSpans: 1 while a run of open cells goes on (stage 1's $FE42)
@equ $FE46 ItemsChanged ; 1 after AddItem $7EA0: RedrawItemsIfChanged $7D66 clears it and redraws the item strip and the count
@equ $FE47 GridNumber ; the map grid the hero is in, 0-10 (EnterGrid10 $969C sets 10, the mummy's room); with RoomNumber it indexes RespawnPoints (x 6) and picks the passages (CheckGridPassages $ACE0)
@equ $FE48 EnergyShown ; the energy the HUD bar last drew
@equ $FE49 EnergyChange ; the pending energy change: $80 and up drains 2 a pass, under $80 refills 2 a pass
@equ $FE4A SpawnDelay ; SpawnTimer $9245: passes to the next random spawn (Random at the stage start; 1 after a room change in grid 10, SavePlayAttrsGrid10 $A19C)
@equ $FE4B FireLatch ; 1 while FIRE stays held after a shot of item kind 1 or 3 (FireKind1 $954B, FireKind3 $959F): one shot a press
@equ $FE4C PiecesTaken ; pieces taken, 0-5
@equ $FE4D PieceFlash ; passes left of the HUD pieces' colour flash
@equ $FE4E PieceTakenFlag ; 1 for one pass after a piece is taken
@equ $FE4F RespawnShiftX ; $FF: no death pending; else the hero's column less the respawn column less 2 (RespawnCountdown $9454); the path flyers move by it (x 2) when their path ends
@equ $FE50 RespawnShiftY ; the hero's line less the respawn line less $27, set with RespawnShiftX
@equ $FE51 HeroFreeze ; passes the hero's state handler is skipped ($17 after a life lost, $7F1D; counted down by HeroUpdate $AE04)
@equ $FE52 TrapChainTimer ; StartTrapChain $82FA sets $1C (grid 3, a rising piece at step $0A); TrapChainStep $830C counts it down and sets grid 3's trap slots 6 to 0 to 1, one every 4 passes
@equ $FE53 PiecesComplete ; set to 1 when the fifth piece is taken; +1 for each item of kind 6 taken (SpawnRewardItem gives the kind-6 item while it is 1)
@equ $FE54 PiecesMask ; one bit a piece of the artefact (the room event's bit, actor +$10): spawned and taken
@equ $FE55 LivesFlash ; the lives boxes' flash step, 0-$10 ($10 idle)
@equ $FE56 GameOverTimer ; 0 in play; 1 when the last life is lost, counts to $32
@equ $FE57 UrnsComplete ; 1 once AltarDisc $8931 finds four of item kind 9 (the urns) carried; then the disc flashes, and item kind 6 selected in grid 1 room 1 at column $15 and up leads into grid 10 (CheckGridPassages $ACE0)
@equ $FE58 BossPhase ; the boss of grid 8 room 2 (a face on the wall that spits shots): 0 asleep, 1 awake and spitting (DrainKind9 $951D sets it when item kind 9 runs out in room 1; HeadShots $B412), 2 beaten (BossBeaten $A24C)
@equ $FE59 BossFlash ; passes left of the boss's hit colours: 2 when a bolt reaches it (UpdateHeroBolt $8148); BossMouth $8AD8 and DrawBossPicture $8F4B count it down
@equ $FE5A BarrierState ; the barrier of grid 0 room 1: 0 closed, 1 its block shot away (BarrierBlockActor $96CB), 2 its pillar sunk: open (BarrierPillarActor $96DD; CheckGridPassages $ACE0 then lets the hero through)
@equ $FE5B BossHits ; the hits the boss still takes: $14 at the stage start (InitStageState $9FE3); -1 for each pass DrawBossPicture $8F57 finds BossFlash set; the last calls BossBeaten $A24C
@equ $FE5D Lives ; lives left, from H at StageEntry
@inline $9163 5
@inline $9193 5
@inline $ABBD
@module variables ; The stage's work space: the play buffer's tail, the shadow attributes, the HUD picture and the records over it
@about The block's first 5057 bytes ($6C3F-$77FF) are loaded with the stage but hold no code. $6C3F-$6CFF is the end of the play buffer PlayBuffer ($5B00-$6CFF: 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear), $6D00-$6FFF the shadow of the screen's attributes. $7000-$76BF holds, as loaded, the HUD: its picture (48 lines of 32 bytes, linear) and its colours (6 rows of 32). StageSetUp $9715 copies the colours into the shadow and dissolves the picture onto the screen (DissolveHud $8FD6); from then on the space is the stage's records: the old room's colours and the burst's particles ($7040), the room's cells ($7280), the hero's and the 13 other actors' records ($74E0, $74F2), the 16 missile records ($75E0), the digit picture ($7640) and the span table ($76A0). EndStage $7898 saves the screen's HUD lines and colours back into $7000 and $7600 before the next stage's block is loaded over them.
@about An actor record (18 bytes, the hero's at $74E0 and 13 at $74F2): +0 X (byte column 0-29; $FF a free record), +1 Y (line in the play buffer), +2 width in bytes, +3 height in lines, +4/+5 the frame's bitmap, +6/+7 the handler, +8 the frame or a counter, +9 flags (bit 0 opaque, bit 4 hit, bit 7 facing left), +$0A the state, +$0B the item kind or a step, +$0C the attribute, +$0D/+$0E the base X and Y (SetActorFrame $ABBD adds the frame's dx, dy to them), +$0F flags (bit 1 kept over a room change, bit 2 a body, bit 6 hidden, bit 7 drawn in the second pass), +$10 the placement's index or a counter, +$11 the pixel shift (1-99 drawn shifted by PreShiftSprite $7F89).
$6C3F s PlayBufferTail ; The last 193 bytes of the play buffer PlayBuffer $5B00-$6CFF (character row 17's last lines)
> ClearBuffer $9A28 clears the play buffer to $6CFF with PUSH HL (SP from $6D00); RoomChange $97FB unpacks the stage's tiles and map into it from $5B00 (stage 4: 5331 bytes, to $6FD2, on over the shadow attributes; RoomCells $9898 takes the map into Cells before RoomChange writes the room's colours); the actors are drawn into it every pass. Zero as loaded. Read and written in s4-right (all 193 bytes).
$6D00 s ShadowAttributes ; The shadow of the screen's 768 attributes, the screen's layout; the play area from $6DC2 (row 6, column 2)
> The HUD's colours are copied into rows 0-5 at the stage's set-up (StageSetUp $9715); RoomChange $97FB writes each cell's attribute into rows 6-23, the actors' colours are painted over them every pass, and UpdateAttributes $91D0 copies the open cells to $5800 (ShowShadowAttributes $91C3 the whole of it). FillShadowAttributes $9193 paints rectangles into it with five bytes after its CALL. Zero as loaded. Read and written in s4-right (all 768 bytes).
$6DC0 PlayAttributes ; row 6: the first row of the play area (the room's 18 rows)
$6DC2 PlayAttributesCell ; row 6, column 2: the room's first cell
$7000 b HudPicture 32 ; The HUD as loaded: 48 lines of 32 bytes (linear, top first), then their colours at $7600 (6 rows of 32)
> DissolveHud $8FD6 dissolves the 48 lines onto the screen's lines 0-47 and StageSetUp $9715 copies the 192 colours into the shadow rows 0-5, once, at the stage's start. EndStage $7898 saves the screen's lines 0-47 back here ($7907, CopyBlockToScreen's reverse) and the attributes $5800-$58BF to $7600 ($78B6), so the next stage's block shows the HUD as the player left it; the copy is CopyBlockToScreen $8FAE called at $7911, which, despite its stage-1 name, copies the screen lines into the block (its LDIR runs after EX DE,HL). Between the two the bytes are the records labelled inside (RoomAttributes, Cells, HeroRecord, Actors, Missiles, DigitBuffer, SpanTable). The picture: the frame of the HUD, the energy bar's box, the score box, the item strip's box, the lives and pieces boxes (docs/img). Read and written in s4-right (all 1728 bytes).
$7040 RoomAttributes ; $7040-$727F: the old room's play colours (SavePlayAttrs $A1A9: 576 bytes, rows 6-23) and the cells' twins ($7042 + row x 32 + column: PutBlock writes 0, UpdateAttributes reads the solid cells' colours); also the burst's particles (StartBurst $A385, 4 bytes each)
$7042 RoomAttributesCell ; the twin of the cell $7282 (576 bytes lower)
$7280 Cells ; the room's cells: 19 rows of 32 (tile numbers, then their kinds after BuildSpans $9959; bit 1 solid, bit 3 deadly, kind 7 a bridge slab)
$7282 CellsPlay ; row 0, column 2: the room's first cell (RoomCells $9898 writes 28 x 18)
$74C0 CellsFloor ; row 18 below the room: 32 bytes of $FF (StartGrid $A5CC), a floor no actor falls through
$74E0 HeroRecord ; the hero's actor record (18 bytes; +0 X)
$74E1 HeroY ; +1 the hero's line
$74E8 HeroFrame ; +8 the frame number of the hero's set
$74E9 HeroFlags ; +9 bit 7: facing left
$74EA HeroState ; +$0A 0 stand, 1 walk, 2 jump, 3 fall, 4 leap back, 5-7 strikes, 9 leap up, $0B recoil, $0F dying (the hero's state handler)
$74EC HeroAttribute ; +$0C the hero's attribute
$74ED HeroBaseX ; +$0D the base column
$74EE HeroBaseY ; +$0E the base line
$74F0 HeroCounter ; +$10 the pause after a death (the hero's death)
$74F2 Actors ; the 13 other actor records, 18 bytes each ($74F2-$75DB); +0 = $FF a free record
$75CA LastActor ; the 13th record
$75DC ActorsEnd ; 4 bytes past the records: only the HUD picture's (DissolveHud, EndStage's save) bytes
$75E0 Missiles ; the 16 missile records, 6 bytes each ($75E0-$763F): +0 the column ($FF free), +1 the line, +2 the kind (MissileHandlers $B4E0), +3 to +5 the kind's own
$7600 HudColours ; the HUD's 192 colours as loaded (rows 0-5); in play the missile records 4-15 lie over them
$7610 MissilesHigh ; missile records 8-15 (AddMissileHigh $B45C: the hero's death sparks)
$7640 DigitBuffer ; in play: the score's digit picture (6 + 2 columns x 8 lines, the score's renderer, RevealScore $97CD) and a sprite's shifted copy (PreShiftSprite $7F89)
$76A0 SpanTable ; in play: the open spans CopyBuffer copies, 6 bytes each (the length, 0, the buffer address, the screen address; SpanCount spans), on to $779B
@res stage4/picture-hud-32x48.bin
$76C0 s SpanTableRest ; The span table's room past the HUD's colours: spans 6-42 ($76C0-$779B)
> BuildSpans $9959 and AddSpan $99E1 write the spans from $76A0 on; a room of many short runs reaches into this space. Zero as loaded. In s4-right 196 of its bytes are written (to $7783) and 31 read.
$779C s Unused779C ; 100 bytes no code reads or writes (s4-right; known only from the code: no operand in the block points into it); zero as loaded
> After SpanTableRest, up to the code at $7800; no instruction of the block names an address in it. Not read or written in any recording (the recordings checked: s4-right, rzx-r4); known only from the code.
@module entry ; The stage's entry and set-up
$7800 c StageEntry ; Start the stage: lives from H, variables, HUD, the first room, then the main loop
> Called by the resident stage loader with H = the lives left. Stores H in Lives, then: InitStageState $9F71 (clears $FE08-$FE5B, the carried items from StartItems, the trap slots $9DAB-$9E1A, the start values), StageSetUp $9715 (the HUD, the score, the item strip), $941C, ResetObjectLists $942B, RoomGrid = $9AE2 (grid 0) with Placements = $9B50, ReviveAllPlacements $A629, $A605, StartGrid $A5CC, RoomEvents $81A8, ClearBuffer $9A28, RunActorHandlers $A746, DrawActors $A768, CopyBuffer $9A4D and $978E; then falls into MainLoop. RoomNumber stays 0 (cleared by InitStageState).
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
@module mainloop ; The main loop and its pass
$7837 c MainLoop ; One pass: pace, HUD, input, actors, draw, copy; SPACE opens the item window
> The pass, in order: PacePass, ShowPieceTaken, FlashPieces, CheckPause (ENTER), SpawnTimer $9245, RedrawItemsIfChanged, ClearBuffer $9A28, CheckStageExit (may leave to StageExit), UpdateMissiles $B4AC, TrapChainStep, RunActorHandlers $A746, LinkTrapSlots, DrawBossPicture, DrawActors $A768, $B412, $A41D, KeyHook, UpdateAttributes (attributes and CopyBuffer), PassTick $97BD (energy, lives flash, game over step), ShowScore, then the SPACE test TestSpaceKey.
> SPACE with CAPS SHIFT (port $FEFE bit 0) ends the stage with E = 1 (QuitStage); SPACE alone opens ItemWindow (stage 1 also refused it while the hero was dying; stage 4 does not test the hero's state). The loop goes on while Lives is not 0 or the hero's state $74EA is not 0; with no lives and the hero back in state 0 it falls into GameOverExit. s4-right ran 945 passes and ended at the game over (217 passes with no lives left before the hero's state came back to 0); rzx-r4 ran 7675 passes, opened the item window 20 times and left through CheckStageExit.
> Witness: L1 8620 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$7878 MainLoopSpace ; SPACE held: CAPS SHIFT too quits, else the item window
$7884 MainLoopNext ; go on while lives are left or the hero is not back in state 0
$7892 c GameOverExit ; No lives: end the stage with E = 0
> Reached from MainLoop when Lives and the hero's state $74EA are both 0. E = 0, then EndStage.
> Witness: L1 1 (s4-right).
$7896 c QuitStage ; CAPS SHIFT + SPACE: end the stage with E = 1
> Reached from MainLoop ($787F) when SPACE and CAPS SHIFT are held. E = 1, then EndStage.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: rzx-r4, s4-right); known only from the code ($787F).
$7898 c EndStage ; Leave the stage: hide the pieces boxes, then EndStageSave (save the HUD, fade) returns E, H = lives, BC = the score's digits
> E (pushed) is the outcome: 0 game over (GameOverExit), 1 quit (QuitStage), 2 stage completed (StageExit $7A72). ClearBuffer $9A28, then the pieces boxes' attributes (rows 3 and 4, columns 25-30: $5879 and $5899, 6 cells each) set to 1 with two LDIRs. Stage 1 hid the lives boxes too with two inline FillAttributes records; stage 4 hides only the pieces boxes and falls straight into EndStageSave.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$78B6 c EndStageSave ; EndStage, continued: save the HUD, clear its fields, fade, return
> Saves the HUD's attributes (rows 0-5, 192 bytes) to $7600. Clears five HUD fields with CopyToScreen from the cleared play buffer $5B00 (stride 0): the score (column 6, line 8, 6 x 8), the fields at column $0E (4 x 8) and column $14 (6 x 8) of line 8, the item strip (column $0A, line $18, 12 x 16) and the pieces field (column $19, line $18, 6 x 16). Then CopyBlockToScreen puts the HUD picture as loaded ($7000, 32 x 48) back on lines 0-47, FlashFadeScreen, ClearScreen, WaitFrames 100. Returns with E = the outcome (popped), BC = ScoreDigitsHigh (the score's six digits as text) and H = Lives.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
@module render ; The renderer: the sprite row plotters, the play buffer, the attributes, ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer
$7929 c FlashFadeScreen ; Fade every coloured ink up to white over 7 frames, then down to black over 7 frames
> Seven times (HALT each): every attribute whose ink is neither 0 nor 7 gets ink + 1. Then seven times (two HALTs each): every ink not 0 gets ink - 1. Inputs: none; changes the whole attribute area $5800-$5AFF. Called by EndStageSave $7914. As in stage 1 at `$7925`.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$792B FadeUpFrame
$7933 FadeUpCell
$793D FadeUpNext
$7948 FadeDownFrame
$7951 FadeDownCell
$7957 FadeDownNext
@module mainloop
$7961 c PacePass ; Pad the pass with a busy wait taken from PaceWaits by grid and room
> BC = PaceWaits[GridNumber x 3 + RoomNumber], then BC is counted down to 0 (PacePassWait, 26 T-states a round). Grid 0 room 0 waits $0258 rounds, grid 0 room 1 $0640, grid 4 rooms 0 and 1 $04B0, every other place 1. Unlike stage 1's PacePass (which also reseeded RandomPointer from R every 64 passes and used DelayBC), stage 4's has its own loop and no reseed. The busy wait ran 1 498 000 rounds in s4-right's 945 passes (grid 0) and 1 099 377 in rzx-r4's 7675.
> Witness: L1 8620 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$797B PacePassWait ; count BC down to 0
$7982 w PaceWaits 8 ; The busy-wait rounds of each place: word GridNumber x 3 + RoomNumber (48 words)
> Read by PacePass $7974 (LD HL,PaceWaits; the word at + 2 x (GridNumber x 3 + RoomNumber)). Words 0 and 1 (grid 0 rooms 0 and 1): $0258 and $0640; words 12 and 13 (grid 4 rooms 0 and 1): $04B0; all the others 1. Three words a grid is fewer than the rooms of some grids (grid 3 has a room 3, grid 4 a room 4), so those rooms read the next grid's words; they are all 1 there. Read every pass in both recordings.
$79E2 c CheckPause ; ENTER pauses: wait for its release, a second press and its release
> Reads port $BFFE bit 0 (ENTER). Not pressed: returns at once. Pressed: waits for the key's release, the next press and its release, so the game stands still between two presses. No other effect. As in stage 1 at `$79B1`. The wait loops from $79EA on ran in neither recording (ENTER never pressed).
> Witness: L1 8620 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$79EA PauseRelease
$79F0 PausePress
$79F6 PauseRelease2
@module render
$79FD c CopyToScreen ; Copy a block of bytes to the screen, line by line
> Inputs: HL = the source, B = the screen column, C = the first pixel line, D = the width in bytes, E = the lines, A = the source's stride (added to HL after each line; 0 repeats one source line, used with the cleared buffer to clear a screen block). Patches the column into the ADD A,n at $7A15 and the stride into the LD C,n at $7A26, then for each line takes the line's address from ScreenLineTable and LDIRs D bytes. Destroys IX, A, BC, DE. Callers: EndStageSave, ShowScore, ShowItemCount, ShowPieceTaken, GameOverStep and the score reveal $97E1, $97F1.
> Witness: L1 9426 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$7A10 CopyToScreenLine
@module hud ; The energy, the lives, the score, the HUD, game over and the stage exit
$7A2D c CheckStageExit ; With item 5 selected, in grid 8 room 1 at columns $10-$13: leave the stage
> Every pass. Only with item 5 selected (GetSelectedItem), in grid 8 (GridNumber) room 1 and with the hero's x ($74E0) from $10 to $13: drops its own return address and runs StageExit (falls into it). Stage 1 tested item 6 at the stage's first room and the hero's y too. Item 5 is the item RoomEvents $8212 gives in grid 9 once the five pieces are taken (SpawnItem with kind 5). In rzx-r4 the whole test passed once, at the end of the run (pass 7675), and the stage was left through StageExit; s4-right never had item 5 selected.
> Witness: L1 8620 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$7A48 c StageExit ; The stage's exit effect: falling stars over a coloured field until FIRE or SPACE, then EndStage with E = 2
> StartStageExit draws the field and seeds 80 stars at $5B00 (4 bytes each); then each frame (HALT) moves the stars of speed 1-3 (MoveStar; a speed-4 star stays), until KeyFire or TestSpaceKey reports a key; then E = 2 and EndStage. As in stage 1 at `$7A1D`, with stage 4's addresses.
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r4).
$7A4C StageExitFrame
$7A53 StageExitStar
$7A70 StageExitDone
$7A75 c MoveStar ; Move one star down by its speed and plot it as two pixel lines
> IX = the star: +0 speed 1-4, +1 the pixel within the byte 0-3, +2 the column 2-29, +3 y ($80 and up: not yet on screen). Off screen: y += speed only. On screen: y = (y + speed) mod 128; IY = ScreenLineTable + 96 + 2y (line 48 + y); clears the star's column on speed lines from there down, then plots the two lines StarPixels[(speed - 1) x 8 + pixel x 2] under them. As stage 1's MoveStar `$7A4A`.
> Witness: L1 5974 (rzx-r4).
$7A83 MoveStarOnScreen
$7A8C MoveStarPlot
$7AB5 MoveStarClear
$7AE6 b StarPixels 8 ; The two pixel lines of a star, by speed (rows 1-4) and pixel (pairs 0-3)
> Read by MoveStar $7AAE (LD HL,StarPixels; + (speed - 1) x 8 + pixel x 2): speed 1 a single pixel, speed 2 two pixels on one line, speeds 3-4 two pixels on two lines. Read in rzx-r4 (the stage exit).
$7B06 c StartStageExit ; Clear the play area, colour it at random and seed 80 stars
> ClearPlayBuffer, then clears 144 screen lines from line 48 (ScreenLineTable + 96), 30 bytes each from column 0; FillAttributes with the inline StageExitBox (columns 2-29, rows 6-23, attribute 0).
