> IY = the hero. Column $1F and up, or 0: LoseLife $7F05. The selected item's kind (GetSelectedItem $7F3F): 1 FireKind1, 3 FireKind3, 9 DrainKind9. Dying (state $0F): RespawnCountdown. Colour +$0C: Energy under $0E: CycleColour AND 7 (flashing); else + 1 a pass up to 7 (white). While HeroFreeze counts down the state handler is skipped. Else by the state +$0A: 0 HeroStand, 1 HeroWalk, 2 HeroJump, 3 HeroFall, 4 HeroLeapBack, 5 HeroStrikeMid, 6 HeroStrikeHigh, 7 HeroStrikeLow, 9 HeroLeap, $0A HeroThrow, $0B HeroRecoil $8B3A. Called from HeroActor `$ABF9`. Stage 1's routine (`$AC3D`) differs in the hazards and weapons.
> Witness: L1 8621 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$AE11 HeroUpdateEdge
$AE14 HeroUpdateItems
$AE45 HeroColourNormal
$AE50 HeroUpdateFreeze
$AE5C HeroUpdateDispatch
$AE97 c HeroThrowMissile ; Throw one of item kind 2: a missile of kind 5 (left) or 6 (right), effect $0B
> Called from HeroThrow `$B080` at its frame 8. GetSelectedItem $7F3F; a count of 0 does nothing, else count - 1, ShowItemCount $7D9E, AddMissile with D = the column (+ 1 facing right), E = the line + 8, C = 5 facing left, 6 facing right (both handled by $8450), B = 1, A = 1, then PlaySoundVector $0B.
> Witness: L1 10 (rzx-r4).
$AEC2 HeroThrowMissileAdd
$AECF c HeroStand ; State 0: read the controls
> IY = the hero. FIRE: HeroFireHeld. DOWN: StartLeap. UP: StartJump. RIGHT: walk right (WalkRight), first turning (base column + 4, facing right) when facing left; LEFT the same to the left (WalkLeft). No key: HeroStandFrame. The keys through the resident's readers $FC90 (UP), $FC9F (DOWN), $FCAE (LEFT), $FCBD (RIGHT), $FCCC (FIRE). As in stage 1 at `$ADA2`.
> Witness: L1 3421 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$AEF5 HeroStandLeft
$AF09 c HeroStandFrame ; Show the standing frame (frame $0C of the walk set) and end the pass
> Frame $0C of HeroStandSet. Also jumped to by the states when they end, by RespawnCountdown `$9474`, EnterGrid10 `$96BD`, PlaceHeroAtStart `$A613` and the grid moves `$8BAF` .. `$8D52`. As in stage 1 at `$ADDD`.
> Witness: L1 311 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$AF11 w HeroStandSet 2 ; SetActorFrame's parameters: the walk frame table $E10B, its graphics $DEA4 (13 frames; $0C stands)
> Inline after HeroStandFrame's CALL SetActorFrame $ABBD. Read in s4-right (17 passes) and rzx-r4 (294).
$AF15 c HeroFireHeld ; FIRE held while standing: a throw (item kind 2) or a strike (item kind 7)
> GetSelectedItem $7F3F: kind 2 StartThrow. Kind 7: DOWN the low strike (state 7, HeroStrikeLow), UP the high strike (state 6, HeroStrikeHigh), LEFT the middle strike (state 5, HeroStrikeMid), each from frame $FF with the base column + 1. Other kinds: nothing. Stage 1's (`$ADE9`) strikes with kinds 6, 5 and 3.
> Witness: L1 285 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
