@module rooms
$B2EC c CellUnderFeet ; HL = the room cell under the actor's feet, E (and D facing left) columns back; Z: not solid
> IY = the actor. The cell row = (line + height + 3) / 8, the column = +0 - E (- D more facing left); HL = row x 32 + column (an offset into the cells $7282). Z when bit 1 (solid) of the cell is clear. As in stage 1 at `$B134`.
> Witness: L1 4069 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$B30D CellUnderFeetColumn
$B31A c CellBelowFeet ; A = the room cell one row below the actor's feet, 4 columns back facing left; NZ: solid (not referenced)
> The cell row (line + height) / 8 + 1, the column +0 (- 4 facing left), HL into $7282. No instruction or word of the image refers to `$B31A`.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s4-right, rzx-r4); known only from the code.
$B33A CellBelowFeetColumn
$B346 c CellAt ; A = the room cell at column E, pixel line D; Z: not solid
> HL = D / 8 x 32 + E - 4 (an offset into the cells $7282). The cell's bits: 1 solid, 3 deadly (CheckDeadlyFloor). As in stage 1 at `$B162`.
> Witness: L1 529 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$B363 c FlashCellWait ; Flash the attribute $58C2 + HL red and yellow until N is pressed (not referenced)
> Saves AF; the attribute at $58C2 + HL alternates $50 and $70 a frame each (HALTs); reads the keyboard half-row $7FFE: N (bit 3) ends it, else the resident's $FCDB is called; the DJNZ's counter is B, which LD BC,$7FFE has just set to $7F. No instruction or word of the image refers to `$B363`.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s4-right, rzx-r4); known only from the code.
$B36A FlashCellLoop
$B37E FlashCellEnd
