@module missiles ; The missiles: shots, thrown objects and flyers in 16 six-byte records at $75E0
$B5C5 c HeadShot ; Missile kind 3: the boss's shot, flying left and up or down by its direction
> IY = the missile (+4 its direction 0-4). Column - 1 a pass (removed at 0); line + HeadShotSteps[+4] (removed at line $88 and down); ShotHitsHero $8607 with C = 2; the image HeadShotImages[+4] drawn (DrawSprite), coloured by HeadShotColour (JP ColourSprite).
> Witness: L1 2288 (rzx-r4).
$B604 b HeadShotImages 4 ; Five image descriptors (address, width, height): $CFB5, $CFC5, $CFD5, $CFE5, $CFF5, each 2 x 8
> Read by HeadShot (LD IX,HeadShotImages + 4 x the direction). Read in rzx-r4 (2178 passes); not in s4-right.
$B618 b HeadShotSteps 5 ; The line change a pass for directions 0-4: -2, 0, 2, 5, 8
> Read by HeadShot (LD HL,HeadShotSteps + the direction). Read in rzx-r4 (2220 passes); not in s4-right.
@module render
$B61D c DrawMissileMirrored ; Draw the image IX points to, mirrored, and colour it
> HL = the image (IX +0/+1), DrawSpriteMirrored, MissileColour, ColourSpriteMirrored. No instruction or word of the image refers to `$B61D`. As in stage 1 at `$B3DA`.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s4-right, rzx-r4); known only from the code.
$B62D b ImageDescriptors 4 ; Nine image descriptors: the image address, the width in bytes, the height in lines
> $E4C3, $E4EA, $E511, $E538 (3 x 13) and $E55F, $E577, $E58F, $E5A7, $E5BF (3 x 8). Only the first two are read: IX = `$B62D` or `$B631` by the bit 0 of the missile's +5 (`$8509`, `$8514`, kinds 5 and 6, the thrown item); the other seven have no reader.
$B651 b SpeedRamps 16 ; Four rows of 16 rising steps 1-5: no reader found (known only from the code)
> No instruction or word of the image refers to `$B651`; it takes the place of stage 1's SpeedSteps (`$B3FA`).
$B691 c ColourSprite ; Fill the attribute shadow under an image with C
> IY = the position, IX the image descriptor (+2 width, +3 height): (height / 8 + 1) rows of the width. As in stage 1 at `$B40A`.
> Witness: L1 5431 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$B6A3 ColourSpriteRow
$B6A8 ColourSpriteCell
$B6B2 c DrawSprite ; Copy an image to the play buffer at the actor's position (no mask)
> HL = the image, IX the descriptor (+2 width in bytes, +3 height in lines), IY the position (BufferAddressHL). The bytes replace the buffer's. As in stage 1 at `$B42B`.
> Witness: L1 2740 (rzx-r4).
$B6B9 DrawSpriteRow
$B6CD c DrawSpriteMirrored ; Copy an image mirrored left to right (through the bit-reverse table $FA00)
> As DrawSprite, each row written from right to left and each byte reversed by the resident's table at $FA00. As in stage 1 at `$B446`.
> Witness: L1 80 (rzx-r4).
$B6D4 DrawSpriteMirroredRow
$B6DF DrawSpriteMirroredByte
$B6F6 c ColourSpriteMirrored ; ColourSprite for a mirrored image (filled leftwards from its right edge)
> As in stage 1 at `$B46F`.
> Witness: L1 80 (rzx-r4).
$B70F ColourSpriteMirroredRow
$B714 ColourSpriteMirroredCell
@module hero
$B71E c CheckDeathZone ; Grid 0 room 1, column $0E and up: the hero loses a life
> Called by HeroActor `$AC02`. GridNumber 0, RoomNumber 1, the hero's column $0E or more: LoseLife (JP $7F05). The barrier stands at column 10 of that room (CheckWalkBarriers $8175 throws him back there until BarrierState is 2).
> Witness: L1 8621 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$B733 c CheckFellOut ; The hero's base line at $51: he loses a life
> IY = the hero (from HeroActor `$ABFC`). +$0E = $51: LoseLife (JP $7F05).
> Witness: L1 8621 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$B73C c CheckDeadlyFloor ; Standing or walking on a deadly cell: drain 4 energy
> IY = the hero (from HeroActor `$ABFF`). States 0 and 1 only: the cell under his feet (as CellUnderFeet with E = 2, D = 0); bit 3 set (the spikes): DamageHero $861B with C = 4.
> Witness: L1 8621 (rzx-r4, s4-right).
$B747 CheckDeadlyFloorCell
$B76C CheckDeadlyFloorColumn
@module rooms
$B77F b StageGraphics 16 ; The stage's tiles, blocks and map, RLE-packed (3366 bytes; 5331 unpacked: 179 tiles, 108 blocks, the nine grids' map)
> RoomChange $97FB unpacks it with Unrle $A5AC to $5B00 at every room change (escape byte $C1). Unpacked: five offset words from $5B0A (the tile kinds 179 bytes, the tile pixels 1432, the tile colours 179, the blocks 108 x 4, the map 3099 bytes: the nine grids in the order of their records, Grid0 25 x 9 first). The unpacked block reaches $6FD2, over the shadow attributes; RoomCells $9898 takes the room's blocks into Cells before RoomChange writes the room's colours. The packer left one stretch of 9 equal bytes unpacked at offset 285 (graphics.txt's `literal`).
> Read in s4-right and rzx-r4 (Unrle: all 3366 bytes, at every room change).
@res stage4/graphics.bin
@module graphics ; The stage's sprites, pictures and their frame tables
@about The stage's graphics $C4A5-$F03E: the sprite sets that SetActorFrame $ABBD reads (two words after its CALL: the frame table, the set's base; the frame records 6 bytes: dx, dy, width in bytes, height in lines, the bitmap's offset from the base; 1 bit a pixel, rows top first, no mask), the plain bitmaps the code addresses itself, the boss's row-packed picture and colours, the burst's tables. Each set's bitmaps are exactly the bytes its frames cover, the table right after them. Each entry is a resource in src/res/stage4/ (README.md there).
$C4A5 b BossPicture 16 ; The boss's face: a row-packed picture of 104 lines (each line a byte LEN x 16 + SKIP, then LEN bytes)
> DrawBossPicture $8F2B draws it with DrawRowPicture $902A into the play buffer at $5F17 every pass in grid 8 room 2 while BossPhase is not 2. Read in rzx-r4 (458 passes); not in s4-right.
@res stage4/rowpicture-boss.bin
$C693 b BossColours 8 ; The boss picture's 8 x 13 attributes, normal
> DrawBossPicture copies them into the shadow at $6E58 (columns $18-$1F, rows 10-22). Read in rzx-r4.
@res stage4/table-boss-colours.bin
$C6FB b BossHitColours 8 ; The boss picture's 8 x 13 attributes while BossFlash runs (a hit)
> DrawBossPicture, instead of BossColours, while BossFlash is set. Read in rzx-r4 (20 hits).
@res stage4/table-boss-hit-colours.bin
$C763 b BrazierSprites 8 ; A brazier's flame: 4 frames (BrazierFrames $892D, Brazier $8917)
> Read in s4-right and rzx-r4.
@res stage4/sprites-brazier.bin
$C825 b TrapSprites 8 ; The traps' set: 27 frames: the crumbling slab 0-8, the spikes 9-16, the falling column 17-18, the dust 19-24 and two more
> The frame table $CB0B with the base $C825 is named by five readers: CrumblingSlabFrames $86FB, SwitchedSpikesFrames $873E, FloorSwitchFrames $87A8, FallingColumnFrames $888B, ColumnDustFrames $890C. Read in rzx-r4 (and the switches' frame in s4-right).
@res stage4/sprites-traps.bin
$CBAD b PendulumSprites 8 ; The pendulum: 15 frames (PendulumFrames $88C0, Pendulum $888F)
> Read in rzx-r4.
@res stage4/sprites-pendulum.bin
$CF29 b ShotSmallBitmap 2 ; A shot, 2 bytes x 5 lines (ShotFrames $8098's first record)
> ShotFrames' record 0. Read by DrawShotRecord $807C for UpdateHeroShot $80CC (C = 0) in rzx-r4 (264 passes); not in s4-right. The other four records ($CF33, $CF42, $CF51, $CF6B) serve UpdateAimedShot $803A only.
@res stage4/bitmaps-shot-small-2x5.bin
$CF33 b ShotUprightBitmaps 1 ; Two shots, 1 byte x 15 lines (ShotFrames)
> ShotFrames' records 1 and 2; read by DrawShotRecord $807C only for UpdateAimedShot $803A, which no recording ran (the recordings checked: s4-right, rzx-r4); known only from the code.
@res stage4/bitmaps-shot-upright-1x15.bin
$CF51 b ShotSlantedBitmaps 2 ; Two shots, 2 bytes x 13 lines (ShotFrames)
> ShotFrames' records 3 and 4; read by DrawShotRecord $807C only for UpdateAimedShot $803A, which no recording ran (the recordings checked: s4-right, rzx-r4); known only from the code.
@res stage4/bitmaps-shot-slanted-2x13.bin
$CF85 b BoltBitmaps 2 ; The hero's bolt: 3 frames of 2 bytes x 8 lines (HeroBoltFrames $8169)
> Read by UpdateHeroBolt in rzx-r4 (the bolts that hurt the boss).
@res stage4/bitmaps-bolt-2x8.bin
$CFB5 b HeadShotBitmaps 2 ; The boss's shots: 5 frames of 2 bytes x 8 lines, one a direction (HeadShotImages $B604)
> Read in rzx-r4.
@res stage4/bitmaps-head-shots-2x8.bin
$D005 b WaterBitmaps 4 ; The water's surface: 3 frames of 4 bytes x 2 lines (WaterRipple $8629 at $8649: $D005 + 8 x the frame)
> Read in s4-right and rzx-r4.
@res stage4/bitmaps-water-4x2.bin
$D01D b GameOverPicture 8 ; GAME OVER: 8 bytes x 8 lines, drawn in the HUD's item strip (GameOverStep $8414 at $8433)
